                    }
                }
            }
            1 -> {
                // Q&A / FAQ Tab
                val bibleQuestionsList = remember {
                    listOf(
                        Triple(
                            "What is the Bible?",
                            "The Bible is a collection of 66 sacred books written by over 40 distinct, divinely inspired authors over a span of 1,500 years. It is divided into the Old Testament (39 books) and New Testament (27 books). It is God's living Word to humanity, guiding us in truth.",
                            "2 Timothy 3:16-17, 2 Peter 1:21"
                        ),
                        Triple(
                            "How do I start reading the Bible?",
                            "It is highly recommended to start with the Gospel of John in the New Testament to understand the life, divinity, grace, and sacrificial love of Jesus Christ. Then proceed to Romans to understand faith, followed by Psalms for devotion, and Genesis to study foundation and creation.",
                            "John 20:31, Romans 10:17"
                        ),
                        Triple(
                            "What is Salvation and Grace?",
                            "Salvation is God's free gift of redemption and eternal reconciliation with Him, secured by Jesus Christ's sacrifice on the cross and victory over death. Grace is God's unmerited favor—we are saved through faith alone, not by our own good deeds.",
                            "Ephesians 2:8-9, Romans 6:23, John 3:16"
                        ),
                        Triple(
                            "Why does God allow trials & suffering?",
                            "While suffering entered the world through human free will and the fall of creation, God is sovereign and works all things for good to those who love Him. Trials build character, patience, refine faith, and help us depend deeply on Him.",
                            "Romans 8:28, James 1:2-4, 1 Peter 5:10"
                        ),
                        Triple(
                            "What is the doctrine of the Trinity?",
                            "The Trinity is the biblical revelation that there is only one God, who eternally co-exists as three distinct, co-equal, and co-eternal Persons: God the Father, God the Son (Jesus Christ), and God the Holy Spirit.",
                            "Matthew 28:19, 2 Corinthians 13:14, John 1:1"
